NAME
    cd - change the working directory

SYNOPSIS
    cd [dir]

DESCRIPTION
    Changes the shell's working directory, which pwd(1) prints and all
    relative paths resolve against. With no argument, cd moves to '/',
    the shell sandbox root (EmuSen's home directory, shared by all
    accounts).

    A leading '/' refers to the shell sandbox root rather than the host
    operating system root. Paths above the sandbox root are rejected,
    regardless of '..' segments. Because cd takes a single directory
    argument, unquoted spaces after cd are joined into that path; quoting
    also works.

EXAMPLES
    cd /Logs
    cd /Games/snes
    cd My Folder
    cd

EXIT STATUS
    0   Directory changed successfully.
    1   Path is outside the sandbox, does not exist, or could not be
        entered.

SEE ALSO
    pwd(1), ls(1), hier(7)
